@startuml feasibility_estimate
title FeasibilityEstimator.estimate - sequential, budget-bounded feasibility verdict

start
:Load graph, build RawRuleTable + coarse/fine models
(same code and constants as production);
if (structural rejection?\n(requireCatalogAcceptable, minimum cells > grid)) then (yes)
  :FAIL, reason = generator's own message
  (no solving needed);
  stop
endif

:Start wall-clock deadline = budget.wallTime;
:Fill every thread with work (see "pick next work");

repeat
  :Wait for next finished attempt
or the deadline;
  :Add it to its stage's evidence
  (trials += 1, successes += solved, keep closest-cost state);
  if (coarse attempt solved?) then (yes)
    :Queue its pattern for refinement;
  endif
  if (refinement attempt solved?) then (yes)
    :Queue its fine pattern for realization;
  endif

  :Per stage: exact binomial bounds low..high
  on per-attempt success rate, at budget.confidence
  (stages with no trials: 0..1);
  :worldFailure range =
  model(high rates) .. model(low rates)
  model = 1 - (1-(1-pC)^200) * (1-(1-pF)^5) * pR
  target 1%, confidence 99%;

  if (worldFailure upper <= target\nAND every stage has trials?) then (yes)
    :PASS;
    :Cancel running attempts;
    stop
  elseif (worldFailure lower > target?) then (yes)
    :FAIL, attach closest coarse failure
    (SizeSlackReport + AdjacencyReport);
    :Cancel running attempts;
    stop
  else (undecided)
    if (deadline passed?) then (yes)
      :BORDERLINE, report both bounds
      + closest failure;
      :Cancel running attempts;
      stop
    endif
  endif

  partition "pick next work for the freed thread" {
    if (no render in flight AND fine pattern waiting
AND no clean render yet?) then (yes)
      :Run RealizationSelector on it
      (max 1 render in flight);
    elseif (coarse pattern waiting for refinement?) then (yes)
      :Run one refinement attempt
      (production steps + schedule, fresh attempt seed);
    elseif (no render in flight AND fine pattern waiting?) then (yes)
      :Run RealizationSelector on it;
    else
      :Run one coarse attempt
      (production 40M steps + schedule,
      next unused attempt seed);
    endif
  }
repeat while (undecided)

note right
  Every attempt uses production's own step budget and schedule,
  so the measured rate IS production's per-attempt rate.
  Bounds are re-checked after every attempt (repeated looks),
  hence a high confidence (99%) to keep false PASS rare.
  Render is single-shot per world: certifying it needs ~460
  clean trials, so PASS certifies coarse + refinement only
  (user decision 2026-10-31); render failures still count
  toward FAIL and block PASS.
  Refinement rate is pooled across coarse patterns: an
  approximation (patterns differ); stated in the verdict.
end note
@enduml
